---
title: Banana and Walnut Bread
description: A moist load made with ripe mashed bananas and chopped walnuts
source: The Complete Bread Book <urn:isbn:0600314146>
author: Lorna Walker & Joyce Hughes
yield: 1%large loaf
course: Dessert
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
prep time: 15m
cook time: 1h
cuisine: British
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- vegetarian
- sweet
- dessert
- snack
- british
---

Grease a #large (11.5" × 4" × 3") loaf tin{}. Pre-heat the oven to 160°C.

Sift the @self-raising flour{450%g} and @salt{0.5%tsp} into a bowl, rub in the @margarine{100%g} until the mixture resembles breadcrumbs and then add the @caster sugar{100%g} and the @walnuts{100%g}(chopped). Mash the @bananas{4} with the @golden syrup{150%g}, and then beat in the @eggs{2}. Stir the banana mixture into the dry ingredients and mix well together. Turn the mixture into the prepared loaf tin.

Bake in the centre of the oven for about ~{1%hour}. Cool in the tin and when cold turn out and serve sliced with butter.

> The cake roughly doubles in height during cooking; do not overfill the tin or place too close to the top of the oven.